    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40264" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quōdam-mŏdo</span></b> , or,
			separated, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quō-dam
			mŏdo</span></b>  (in tmesi: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quodam tamen modo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 12, 5</span></i>
			), adv.
			quidam-modus, <i>in a certain manner</i>,
				<i>in a measure</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quodammodo latebat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep.
					Eum. 7, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">voce, motu, formā etiam magnifica et
					generosa quodammodo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 75, 261</span></i>
			. diligamus, <i><span class="en">id. Lael. 8, 28</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id. de Or 1, 59, 251</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
